# Artifacts / large data.
#
# EXCEPTION: artifacts/ holds everything needed to CLONE AND RUN this repo
# without the ~50GB raw CIC-IDS2017 release, which is not redistributable
# here and which judges/reviewers are not expected to download:
#
#   artifacts/weights/*.pt      5 ensemble checkpoints (~5.7MB)
#   artifacts/scaler/*          fitted RobustScaler + SHAP background (~44KB)
#   artifacts/processed/*.parquet  windowed, labelled per-day tables (~28MB)
#   artifacts/metrics/**        the published evaluation numbers
#   artifacts/metadata/**       dataset/model/experiment provenance
#
# Inference needs the exact scaler the model was trained against, so the
# weights alone would not be usable; evaluation needs the windowed tables,
# which are derived from the raw release and cannot be rebuilt without it.
# nidra/train/pipeline.py resolves each day from its cached table first and
# only falls back to the raw CSV on a miss, so a clone with these files
# needs no dataset download. Total committed artifact weight is ~34MB.
#
# Still ignored: the experiment trees for rejected variants below (their
# metadata is committed for provenance; the weights run nothing).
artifacts_mvp_2017/weights/*.pt
artifacts_mvp_2017/scaler/*.joblib
artifacts_mvp_2017/scaler/*.npy
artifacts_mvp_2017/processed/
artifacts_logvar15/weights/*.pt
artifacts_diverse/

# Windowed parquet is ignored by default (it is derived data and can be
# large) EXCEPT the production tables above, which ship with the repo.
*.parquet
!artifacts/processed/*.parquet

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# Experiment runs (nidra/scripts/run_experiment.py): the config, provenance
# record, metadata and benchmark JSON of every run are committed; the weights,
# scaler arrays and per-row score dumps are not (they are reproducible from
# the record, and the shipped ones live under artifacts/).
experiments/runs/**/*.pt
experiments/runs/**/*.npy
experiments/runs/**/*.npz
experiments/runs/**/*.joblib
# Disk copy of the Δ=30 run-7 weights; the same bytes are in git under the
# `baseline-delta30-run7` tag (ml/artifacts/weights at that commit).
experiments/baseline_delta30_run7/artifacts/
